{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793706012,"nonce":"BVcjd9YAqSCqkj2R7N9bflCv230=","message":"Progress bar: root cause found and fixed in the working tree (uncommitted). The indeterminate bar's pulse is a composite-promoted CSS animation. Its ancestors' clips (the scroll viewport and the track) were captured as one AABB for the blit, and ambient_clip_rounded returned None when those clips did not overlap, which the blit reads as no clip. A bar scrolled wholly out of the viewport therefore drew unclipped over the fixed header (the track itself is clipped as a normal primitive). Fix: non-overlapping clips give a zero-size clip and composite_replay skips the blit. Repro: blinc_recorder/tests/cn_progress_clip.rs an_indeterminate_bar_scrolled_under_a_header_is_not_drawn_over_it (236 stray pixels before, 0 after); the bar's opacity pulses, so the test checks for any pixel that is not the header colour, not the bar's colour. Spinner under a Toast: not reproduced headless at 1x or 2x, with one or two toasts, a viewport-culled scroll, and full and fast paint (cn_progress_clip a_spinner_under_a_toast_*). Only the spinner's rotating arc draws over the toast in the owner's screenshots, the static track does not, so the arc's layer is composited after the overlay in the window. Still open.","files":null}]}